sweet-diag-exit-ufs-vm (lowclk 2026-11-14, group A items A6-1 and A13-1; research docs/research/160-kernel-cpu-users-lskdd-boot-reads.md s.2, s.3, s.5; tracker L-25): three read-only diagnostics. NO HARDWARE ACCESS, no state change, no new register or command.
(a) New bsd/dev/sweet_exitlog.c (+ bsd/conf/files): the SWEET exec site in kern_exec.c counts execs per process name; exit_with_reason (kern_exit.c, once per process, after p_exit_reason and p_xstat are set and before proc_prepareexit) prints for a name exec'd MORE than 10 times, for its first 5 exits and then every 100th: `SWEET EXIT: NAME[PID] ppid P life_ms L exec_n E exit_n N xstat 0xRV code C signal S reason ns A code 0xB jetsam_flags 0xF by KNAME[KPID]`. rv = the exit status word (signal bits 0..6, exit code = the signed status >> 8, so a negative main() return shows as a negative `code` (sel_code), as kern_exit.c W_EXITCODE forms it); reason = p_exit_reason (namespace OS_REASON_JETSAM = 1, bsd/sys/reason.h:88; code = the jetsam cause); jetsam_flags = the P_JETSAM_* bits exit_with_reason was given; by = current_proc() (the process itself for exit()/a crash, another for a kill); life_ms from p_stats->ps_start (mach time of the fork, kern_fork.c:1121; includes the xpcproxy part for a launchd job). One row when a name passes 10 execs; a full table (768 names; 48 filled at boot on hardware, resident-233035-b4) is a SWEET GAP row. Explains lskdd [obs research 160 s.2: new pid every 1.024 s, no exit row].
(b) CPUSTAT `ufs` row: sweet_ufs_stat gets 4 slots ([6] read bytes, [7] write bytes, [8] read ios, [9] write ios; sweet_ufs.c, after the existing `sweet_ufs_stat[2] += count`, direction = the same `rd` the function already computed). The old fields (`ios cmds KiB busy lockwait maxcmd`, KiB = reads + writes) keep name and meaning; `rios wios rKiB wKiB` are appended at the end of the row.
(c) CPUSTAT vm row every 10 s (every second tick of the 5 s cpustat thread; off with sweetcpustat=0): `CPUSTAT vm up MS ms window MS ms | pageins N pageouts N compressions N decompressions N swapins N swapouts N` (pages, delta since the previous row; first row since boot), read with counter_load of vm_statistics_pageins/pageouts/compressions/decompressions/swapins/swapouts (declared in sweet_cpustat.c with SCALABLE_COUNTER_DECLARE as osfmk/kern/host_statistics.h:45-57 does, because that header is not an installed private header; the counters host_statistics64 HOST_VM_INFO64 returns through get_host_vm_stats, osfmk/kern/host.c:138-150), lock-free.
Host test: tools/test_sweet_diag362.py compiles the pure table logic of sweet_exitlog.c from this patch text (thresholds, every-100th, table full, whole-name match) and checks every hook by text with a mutant per check. NOT compiled as kernel code on the host: the kernel build (tools/xnu-local-build) is the compile check. Not run on hardware.
